//!
//! The queue has a fixed capacity. Producers submit work items; consumers
//! (workers) pull items and execute them. Dropping the queue's handle
//! cancels outstanding work, and each item can also be cancelled while
//! queued (before a worker picks it up) via a per-item `CancellationToken`.

